{"id": "EUVD-2026-80701", "enisaUuid": "0c731be0-5a22-3793-af6e-ede2140df9f8", "description": "MikroTik RouterOS before 7.24 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the userspace SMB daemon that allows unauthenticated attackers to read beyond the end of the request buffer by supplying a crafted uniPwdLen field value in a minimal SMB1 SessionSetupAndX frame. The out-of-bounds read occurs in the SessionSetupAndX handler before any credential validation, potentially exposing sensitive memory contents.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T13:07:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T15:20:03", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://forum.mikrotik.com/t/7-24-stable-is-released/272381", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/mikrotik-routeros-out-of-bounds-read-via-smb1-sessionsetupandx"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-56719", "GHSA-w9p3-2qvw-6779"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.39, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07173f74-8a02-3c7a-bd2b-09348cd7a9c9", "product": {"name": "RouterOS", "vendor": {"name": "MikroTik"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0 \u22647.11.2"}, {"id": "235da824-0128-3942-b370-1a813a46577a", "product": {"name": "RouterOS", "vendor": {"name": "MikroTik"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.49.18"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0fa309cc-f6e2-37a8-bdf6-badbfd7da128", "vendor": {"name": "MikroTik"}}], "isExploited": false}